    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "How much pocket money do you get from your parents every month? What do you often do with your money?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "We asked three British middle school students for their opinions on pocket money."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Ruth Sawyers: I get 5 pounds from my parents every week. I usually save 1.5 pounds and spend the rest."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Generally, the two things I like to buy with my pocket money are "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tracksuits",
            "zh": "运动服"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and trainers. I try to get the same stuff as my friends."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I don’t really think about getting a raise. And I don’t usually talk about pocket money with my friends at school. If some people’s parents give them too much pocket money, other children might get "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "jealous",
            "zh": "妒忌的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It’s important not to show off what you’ve got."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Maya Varsani: I get 6 pounds from my mum and 8 pounds from my dad every month. I try to save and buy presents for my family. This year, I bought my mum a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "lipstick",
            "zh": "唇膏"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for 9.5 pounds for Mother’s Day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I also often spend my pocket money on CDs. I like the idea of having my own money to spend."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Jimmy Segalov: My mum gives me 10 pounds a week. She says I can either spend it at the school canteen or she will make me a packed lunch (and then I can spend the 10 pounds on whatever I want)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p9",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I like Nike trainers. If something costs 50 pounds and I only have 40, my mum might give me 10 more. Sometimes I have to do housework to earn extra money."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p10",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I know some parents can’t afford to give their kids much pocket money. Therefore, I try not to talk about my pocket money at school."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
